From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OpenMCX <noreply@openmcx.invalid>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] presence_reginfo: the first NOTIFY of a subscription made
 just after a re-registration has the new registration

After a network-initiated deregistration with the event "deactivated"
(reginfo.deregister) the UE registers again at once (TS 24.229 clause
5.4.1.5) and subscribes to its reg event. The presence module stores the
final document of the deregistration (every registration terminated), sends
its NOTIFYs and only then removes it (patch 0009). A UE that registered again
within some 15 ms of the NOTIFY it got subscribed while that document was
still stored, and patch 0009 kept a final document as the first NOTIFY of a
subscription: the new subscription got the old binding, terminated with the
event "deactivated" and its old callid, and was ended by it.

- presence_reginfo reginfo_body_setversion(): the first document sent to a
  subscriber is the registrar's state (reginfo_current_body) whenever the
  registrar has a contact of the AOR, also when the stored presentity is a
  final document; a final document is kept while the registrar has no
  contact (it then reports the end of the registration). TS 24.229 clause
  5.4.2.1.2: the first NOTIFY has "the state information of all registered
  public user identities of the user".

The modified file carries a notice of the change (GPL-2.0 section 2(a)).
---
diff --git a/src/modules/presence_reginfo/notify_body.c b/src/modules/presence_reginfo/notify_body.c
index 9f07e66..2f2ae9b 100644
--- a/src/modules/presence_reginfo/notify_body.c
+++ b/src/modules/presence_reginfo/notify_body.c
@@ -32,6 +32,9 @@
  * Modified by OpenMCX on 2026-11-26 (GPL-2.0 section 2(a)): the first document sent to a subscriber, and a document
  * when no presentity is stored, has the registrar's current contacts (pua_reginfo's reginfo_current_body): the
  * stored presentity can lag the registrar (TS 24.229 clause 5.4.2.1.2, full state).
+ * Modified by OpenMCX on 2026-11-26 (GPL-2.0 section 2(a)): the first document of a subscription is the registrar's
+ * also when the stored presentity is a final document but the registrar has a contact again (a user who registered
+ * again at once after a network-initiated deregistration).
  */
 
 /*! \file
@@ -395,14 +398,21 @@ int reginfo_is_final_body(str *body)
  * 5.1). The first document sent to the subscriber is the registrar's state
  * (full state, TS 24.229 clause 5.4.2.1.2): the stored presentity can still be
  * the one before a REGISTER whose PUBLISH is not yet stored. A final document
- * (every registration terminated) is kept: it reports the end of the
- * registration.
+ * (every registration terminated) is kept while the registrar has no contact
+ * of the AOR: it reports the end of the registration. When the registrar has
+ * a contact again, the final document is the one of a registration that ended
+ * before this subscription: a user deregistered by the network with
+ * "deactivated" registers again at once (clause 5.4.1.5) and subscribes while
+ * the presence module still holds that document (it is removed only once its
+ * NOTIFYs are sent), and the new subscription's first NOTIFY would carry the
+ * old binding, terminated, and end the subscription. It gets the registrar's
+ * state.
  */
 str *reginfo_body_setversion(subs_t *subs, str *body)
 {
 	str *current = NULL, *versioned;
 
-	if(subs->version <= 1 && body && !reginfo_is_final_body(body))
+	if(subs->version <= 1 && body)
 		current = reginfo_registrar_body(&subs->pres_uri);
 	if(current == NULL)
 		return reginfo_body_setversion_doc(subs, body);
